<title>USA: DOT July report of U.S. airline performance.</title>
<headline>DOT July report of U.S. airline performance.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Transportation Department Air Travel Consumer Report on the performance of the 10 largest U.S. air carriers in domestic non-stop flights.</p>
<p>    ON-TIME ARRIVALS - -   COMPLAINTS - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>    Percent Arriving	 Total Number Per   Mishandled Bags/</p>
<p>    On Time Per Carrier    100,000 Passengers  1,000Passengers</p>
<p> -	  July96  June96   July96   July95     July96  July95</p>
<p> Alaska     65.3   67.3     0.85    0.20	 8.38     7.15</p>
<p> Amer.West  67.7   68.9     1.34    1.03	 4.81     5.17</p>
<p> American   65.3   69.4     1.16    0.47	 5.10     4.94</p>
<p> Cont.'l    74.3   71.0     0.77    0.91	 4.33     4.40</p>
<p>    ON-TIME ARRIVALS - -   COMPLAINTS - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>    Percent Arriving	 Total Number Per   Mishandled Bags/</p>
<p>    On Time Per Carrier    100,000 Passengers  1,000Passengers</p>
<p> -	  July96  June96   July96   July95     July96  July95</p>
<p> Delta	74.8   75.6     1.08    0.53	 4.92     5.32</p>
<p> Northwest  79.0   74.6     1.06    0.69	 4.55     7.39</p>
<p> Southwest  87.0   84.1     0.23    0.13	 3.89     4.28</p>
<p> TWA	  66.5   68.2     1.64    1.12	 5.77     5.07</p>
<p> United     76.4   74.4     0.94    0.69	 6.57     4.34</p>
<p> USAir	77.0   76.6     1.13    0.56	 5.14     4.97</p>
<p> Total	75.3   74.7     1.00    0.59	 5.17     5.11</p>
<p>The percent of on-time arrivals is based on reports from the 27 airports required to report by the DOT plus voluntary reports from other airports.</p>
<p>The consumer complaints portion of the report is based on complaints made to DOT in writing, by telephone or in person. DOT said it has not determined the validity of the complaints.</p>
<p>Total passenger complaints include flight delays, mishandled bags and oversales. They do not concern charges of safety violations, which are handled by the Federal Aviation Administration.</p>
